{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Homotopy.HomotopyGroup","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.Prod.serreCubePairBridge_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.Prod.serreCubePairBridge_fst","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyLifting.lean#L215-L220","doc":"The bridge holds for a trivial bundle — because there the relative property\nholds unconditionally. Not evidence for the general case; evidence that the\nstatement is the right shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.SerreCubePairBridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.SerreCubePairBridge","kind":"def","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyLifting.lean#L197-L213","doc":"**The unproved bridge**, stated so that it has a name.\n\nFor a fibration, the plain homotopy lifting property against a cube implies\nthe stationary relative property against that cube and its boundary. The\nproof is the pair homeomorphism `(Iⁿ × I, Iⁿ × {0} ∪ ∂Iⁿ × I) ≅ (Iⁿ × I,\nIⁿ × {0})` obtained by projecting radially from a point above the cube\n(Hatcher, §4.2). It is real geometry, it is **not proved here**, and no\nresult in this development invokes it — `FibrationExactness` assumes the\nrelative property directly instead.\n\nRecorded as a `Prop`-valued definition rather than a `sorry`ed theorem on\npurpose: a `sorry` would leak `sorryAx` into every downstream axiom check\nand make the honest results indistinguishable from the assumed one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.Prod.isHurewiczFibration_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.Prod.isHurewiczFibration_fst","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyLifting.lean#L190-L193","doc":"Hence a trivial bundle is a Hurewicz fibration, and so a Serre one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.Prod.hasHomotopyLiftingProperty_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.Prod.hasHomotopyLiftingProperty_fst","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyLifting.lean#L184-L188","doc":"The absolute form of the same fact, for reference and for the composition\nlemma. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.Prod.hasHomotopyLiftingPropertyRel_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.Prod.hasHomotopyLiftingPropertyRel_fst","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyLifting.lean#L166-L182","doc":"**A trivial bundle is a fibration**, and it satisfies the *relative*\nproperty as well, for every pair `(Y, A)`.\n\nThis is the theorem that makes everything downstream non-vacuous. The\nrelative HLP is taken as a hypothesis by the exactness result, and a\nhypothesis nothing satisfies proves nothing; here it is discharged\noutright. The lift is the only available one — carry the homotopy in the\nbase coordinate and hold the fibre coordinate fixed at whatever `f`\nchose — and holding the fibre coordinate fixed is exactly why the boundary\ndoes not drift. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.HasHomotopyLiftingProperty.comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.HasHomotopyLiftingProperty.comp","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyLifting.lean#L147-L158","doc":"Fibrations compose. The proof is the only thing one would guess: lift the\nhomotopy through the outer map first, then lift the result through the\ninner one, whose start is already lifted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.hasHomotopyLiftingProperty_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.hasHomotopyLiftingProperty_id","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyLifting.lean#L138-L145","doc":"The identity has the homotopy lifting property: the homotopy is its own\nlift. Trivial, and it is the first check that the definition is not\naccidentally empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.hasHomotopyLiftingPropertyRel_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.hasHomotopyLiftingPropertyRel_empty","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyLifting.lean#L124-L136","doc":"With `A = ∅` the relative property is exactly the absolute one: the extra\nhypothesis and the extra conclusion are both vacuous. Recorded so the\nrelative predicate is visibly a *refinement* of the plain one rather than an\nunrelated definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.IsHurewiczFibration.isSerreFibration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.IsHurewiczFibration.isSerreFibration","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyLifting.lean#L120-L122","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.IsSerreFibration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.IsSerreFibration","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyLifting.lean#L114-L118","doc":"A **Serre fibration**: the homotopy lifting property against the cubes\n`Iⁿ`. This is the version tied to `π_n`, because `Mathlib`'s `GenLoop` is\nbuilt out of maps from `Fin n → I`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.IsHurewiczFibration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.IsHurewiczFibration","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyLifting.lean#L108-L112","doc":"A **Hurewicz fibration**: the homotopy lifting property against every space\nin the universe `w`. Universe-polymorphic rather than fixed at `Type 0`\nbecause the spaces this corpus builds do not all live in one universe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.HasHomotopyLiftingPropertyRel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.HasHomotopyLiftingPropertyRel","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyLifting.lean#L88-L106","doc":"**The stationary relative homotopy lifting property** with respect to a pair\n`(Y, A)`.\n\nSame data as `HasHomotopyLiftingProperty`, with one hypothesis and one\nconclusion added: if `H` is *constant in `t`* on `A`, the lift may be chosen\nconstant in `t` on `A` too.\n\nThis is what the fibration exactness argument needs and the plain HLP does\nnot give. Lifting a nullhomotopy of `p ∘ g` produces a map `Iⁿ → E` into the\nfibre, but with no control on `∂Iⁿ` the result is not a based sphere at all\n— the boundary drifts away from the basepoint along the lifted homotopy, and\nthe class it would represent does not exist. Pinning the boundary is not a\nconvenience; without it there is no theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.HasHomotopyLiftingProperty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting.HasHomotopyLiftingProperty","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyLifting.lean#L75-L86","doc":"**The homotopy lifting property** of `p : E → B` with respect to a space `Y`.\n\nGiven a homotopy `H : I × Y → B` and a map `f : Y → E` lifting its start,\nthere is a homotopy `H' : I × Y → E` lifting all of `H` and starting at `f`.\n\nThe argument order `I × Y` (rather than `Y × I`) is deliberate: it is the\norder `ContinuousMap.Homotopy` uses, so a Mathlib homotopy can be fed to\nthis predicate with no shuffling. Nothing about the definition depends on\nit, and everything about the usability does. ","signatureChunk":0}]}